# persona's own nginx stream-backend entry — see cinder's own
# deploy/README.md "MULTI-REPO OWNERSHIP" note. This repo owns and
# ships exactly this file; it must never gain another repo's hostname
# lines, and no other repo's fragment should ever gain this one.
#
# One hostname — the landing page — reverse-proxied by nginx's shared
# stream{} passthrough straight through to persona-caddy, which
# terminates TLS itself (see cinder's D007 for why nginx never
# terminates TLS here).
#
# Port is a placeholder, not just the domain — must match
# deploy/docker-compose.yml's own published persona-caddy HTTPS port
# exactly.
#
# .template, not .map: deploy/configure-nginx.sh runs this through
# `envsubst`, restricted to exactly the placeholders below.

${PERSONA_DOMAIN}   127.0.0.1:${PERSONA_CADDY_HTTPS_PORT};  # persona-caddy (landing page)
